  "description": "Certificate of lawfulness for the existing single storey rear extension to the house",
  "development_type": "Certificates of Lawful Development",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 3 March 2026, the single storey rear extension at 298 Great West Road as shown on the drawing(s) submitted on 3rd March 2026 and numbered Unnumbered planning statement, unnumbered location plan, B101, B102, B103, B104, B107, B108 was not lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development fails to comply with the terms of Class A Clause G Part i of Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended), and Class A, Clause A Part i of Part 2 of Schedule 2 because the extension would extend beyond the rear wall by more than 6 metres, and the blockwork walls would exceed a height of 2 metres above ground level, respectively."
